bec129247c3e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89911638?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bdiadiun","id":89911638,"login":"bdiadiun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTExNjM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bdiadiun/artifact-synchronization/commits/bf250b834d981d0da9fbc73143a9096709e5a643/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T10:29:51Z","email":"b.diadiun@gmail.com","name":"Bohdan Diadiun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T10:29:51Z","email":"b.diadiun@gmail.com","name":"Bohdan Diadiun"},"message":"refactor: two applications, one useChannel\n\nThe channel package holds one end of the channel per window, created when\nits module loads, and offers `useChannel(options)` to both applications: it\nnames the peer on the first mount, leases the window listener per mount and\nsubscribes the caller to `{ ready, queued }`. The interface is\n`{ send, on, getState }`; `createChannel`, `onMessage`, `dispose`,\n`subscribe` and the `announcements` counter are gone (A-34).\n\nBoth applications connect the same way: `useChannel`, then\n`channel.on(handler)` in an effect. The form''s actions are the contract''s\ncommands and `dispatch` sends them before it reduces; the OHIF-side\napplication subscribes to OHIF with `ohif.on(handler)`, whose facade parses\nthe measurement object once, throttles updates per uid and delivers events\nin the contract''s shape; `handleOhif` mirrors `handleCommand`.\n\nFixes from the review (A-33): `MEASUREMENT_UPDATED` keeps its geometry, a\nrestore mark is cleared once it stops being true, `VIEWER_READY` is\nanswered with the rows on screen, a standalone viewer posts nothing, the\nstored envelope names `studyInstanceUid`, `viewer:link` links our packages\nonly, lint covers the packages'' `.tsx`, and `complexity` counts a switch\nonce. Tests follow the code or go where their subject went.","tree":{"sha":"3bee1cb89613d20ec2f4a2eb10d899f0ba7b2e25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bdiadiun/artifact-synchronization/git/trees/3bee1cb89613d20ec2f4a2eb10d899f0ba7b2e25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bdiadiun/artifact-synchronization/git/commits/bf250b834d981d0da9fbc73143a9096709e5a643","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89911638?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bdiadiun","id":89911638,"login":"bdiadiun","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTExNjM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdiadiun","user_view_typ