i.github.com/users/kuh9325/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/commits/06842465d58b0175234ef488086f3bfd61c6133d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T09:54:08Z","email":"kuh9325@naver.com","name":"Junho Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T09:54:08Z","email":"kuh9325@naver.com","name":"Junho Kim"},"message":"script VM + collision: P1 batch-2 — 0x9d/0x9e/0x9f/0xb6 recovered, boxTri escape fix\n\nFour counted-seam opcodes fully recovered from BUILD_A disasm and\nimplemented with observed semantics:\n\n- 0x9d (0x44880e) repel impulse: named+spawnId scan of the home-arena\n  +0x68 list; ctx velocity = (ctx.pos - tgt.pos) * speed/|d|, +0xec\n  path unbound.\n- 0x9e (0x44f453 -> FUN_00454c6c) damage/event volume: ctx +0x198\n  AABB rescaled by +0x2c0; flags1&1 player-damage element overlap,\n  flags1&2 sibling mark/wake/health sweep, flags2&1 self-kill,\n  flags2&2 +0x108=imgref goto (no null normalisation). Cleared as the\n  collision-escape candidate — damage/event semantics only.\n- 0x9f (0x449614 -> FUN_004549b4) scripted FX spawn: mode-0/1/2\n  position (ctx pos / yaw-rotated offset / inline), FUN_00403538\n  procedural record, +0x108=imgref script PC, +0x316..322 params.\n- 0xb6 (0x4474a2) indexed conditional goto: trunc via FUN_0047d59a\n  (RC=11 — toward zero, not round-to-nearest); in-range consumes\n  op0+op1 and gotos op1 (0 -> halt via base-normalised null),\n  out-of-range consumes one u32 and falls through. Dead-read loop\n  quirk reproduced.\n\nShared-table fallback fixes:\n\n- eventLatch.arena (ctx +0x60 home arena) is now wired at load and\n  inside the fallback — shared ops walking +0x60->+0x68 (0x9d, 0x9e\n  flags1&2, 0xe9) previously saw a null arena through arena contexts.\n- Focused mirror tests: in/out field copy, linkage propagation,\n  isolation, no stale accumulation, failure paths, suspend/resume PC\n  checkpoint round-trip.\n- Real shared-op regions exercised via --script-pc QA entry (dev\n  tool): +124a8 (HMO_5 XG1 combat block, settles into poll loop),\n  +105ac and +d099 (authentic Gosub-underflow callee kills).\n\nCollision (the owner-reported escape mechanism, OBSERVED in\nFUN_004089c0): boxTri''s diff&2 branch — when an edge crosses the +a0\nface and the crossing coordinate is inside the other extent, the\noriginal breaks the edge scan and the axis PASSES. The port broke\ninto `if (mask != 0) return 0` and reported separation, so swept\nboxes fell through floors whose projected edges straddle the box\nface. Fixed (mask=0 before break); the mdk-inspect census replica\nmirrors it.\n\n--collision-census (QA dev mode): per-arena attach + 45-frame settle,\nflag census (0x10 render-skip vs 0x20 collision-skip — zero\nrenderNoCollide polys anywhere; the flag asymmetry is NOT the escape\nmechanism), object census, 2-unit support grid, per-hole BSP descent\ntrace + boxTri replica + stepped probes. Interior unsupported cells:\n2308 -> 267 (-88%); residual = 39 legit voids + 55 stepped-hit\n(column-sweep slide-off artefacts; per-frame support exists) + 1\ndown-facing-poly slide-off.\n\nRegression: mdk_tests 583,499/0; frontend 340/0; ctest 1/1; pytest\n33/0/0; save/restore, campaign, mode-5, combat smokes clean; L5-L7\ngoldens byte-exact; L4/L8 intentionally drift (global collision\nsemantics corrected — old goldens NOT overwritten); freefall c0-c4\nbyte-identical to f692ec6 (freefall does not consume the collision\npath). L3 golden remains superseded; no new golden minted.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-i