plant/commits/b8beedd730747d9a3be82c85f95a0ebe454ec75f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:15:02Z","email":"kuh9325@naver.com","name":"Junho Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:15:02Z","email":"kuh9325@naver.com","name":"Junho Kim"},"message":"Phase 17A checkpoint: traversal combat presentation foundation\n\nPhase 17A is NOT closed — this is an intermediate checkpoint of the\nGodot presentation half of the reconstructed G4 combat system.\n\nImplemented (presentation-only, semantics stay in the native core):\n\n- Player projectile presentation: scoped shot pool snapshots, KURT\n  world meshes (class-table slot 1 resolves via STREAM/STREAM.BNI,\n  re-headed with the slot-byte flag like the original EDX arg),\n  bullet-cam SubViewport windows, HUD shot-slot indicators.\n- Enemy projectile presentation contract: classIdx >= 0 resolves the\n  level enemy-table model; the shot snapshot carries the fields the\n  presenter needs (pos/tail, yaw/pitch, spin, render scalar, ribbon,\n  hud frame, arena).\n- Impact FX: wall/object impact events carry pos/normal/arena;\n  FUN_00404108 shard burst presentation with the decoded init\n  (tetra verts + jitter, up-biased velocity), contact-bounce via\n  fx_stab, and the 60+(rand>>9) countdown reap.\n- Detonation/explosion presentation: kDetonation events carry the\n  FUN_004575fc camera-facing transform + scale; remnant nodes.\n- Enemy/object death + corpse/remnant presentation: death-script\n  handoff (kind 5), teardown (kind 6) with the 16-shard burst and\n  the EXPLODE corpse scaled by victim/explode z-span.\n- Diagnostics: bridge diagnostic_kill/diagnostic_shockwave exercise\n  the authentic objectDieFacingPlayer / fxShockwave seams.\n\nThe combat Godot smoke checks themselves pass (all 25). One\nnon-combat texture-cache bound assertion in the damage/death window\nremains flaky (delta 52..119 vs the arbitrary <64 bound; the real\ncontract is the 4096-entry bounded cache). L6/L8 Godot combat\nvalidation and the full regression pass remain pending.\n\nNo gameplay/damage/collision/AI/script/timing semantics changed;\nall core additions are presentation-contract fields and read-only\nmodel resolvers. mdk_tests: 5679 checks, 0 failures.\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5ced9d37529aebb96684458d0769d614b21868e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/git/trees/5ced9d37529aebb96684458d0769d614b21868e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/git/commits/b8beedd730747d9a3be82c85f95a0ebe454ec75f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18028674?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kuh9325","id":18028674,"login":"kuh9325","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDI4Njc0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/commit/b8beedd730747d9a3be82c85f95a0ebe454ec75f","node_id":"C_kwDOUdj5udoAKGI4YmVlZGQ3MzA3NDdkOWEzYmU4MmM4NWY5NWEwZWJlNDU0ZWM3NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/commit/d0f9d8494aea1b765fd9dac27fcfa78f7375b82e","sha":"d0f9d8494aea1b765fd9dac27fcfa78f7375b82e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/commits/d0f9d8494aea1b765fd9dac27fcfa78f7375b82e"}],"sha":"b8beedd730747d9a3be82c85f95a0ebe454ec75f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/commits/b8beedd730747d9a3be82c85f95a0ebe454ec75f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18028674?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kuh9325","id":18028674,"login":"kuh9325","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDI4Njc0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/commits/d0f9d8494aea1b765fd9dac27fcfa78f7375b82e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T05:56:53Z","email":"kuh9325@naver.com","name":"Junho Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T05:56:53Z","email":"kuh9325@naver.com","name":"Junho Kim"},"message":"Phase 16C (Presentation): freefall Kurt Godot presentation\n\nPresent mode-2 freefall in the Godot frontend end to end: the real\nFALL3D models driven by the shared object-anim driver on per-object\npresentation twins, the FALL3D_<course>.MTI material bank, the\nFALLP_<course> palette, and the FUN_004123f4 fixed-orientation\ncamera — gameplay stays authoritative in the native runtime, Godot\nconsumes bridge snapshots only.\n\nCore (src/core):\n- freefall_scene (new): loads FALL3D.BNI + FALL3D_<c+1>.MTI +\n  FALLP_<c+1>; resolves the 23-entry roster (0x49a67c names +\n  0x49a664 flag bytes — bit7 = named-element records, low 7 = the\n  0x88-stride model-slot index); re-heads the flag-less records\n  with the roster flag and decodes via the shared FUN_00428400\n  port; deep-copies prototypes into per-pool-slot DynamicObject\n  twins stepped by the real driver; binds KURTANIM/KURT_HIT/\n  BONESANM on the runtime''s anim handles and mirrors the hit-anim\n  rebind at the -256 sentinel; materials resolve texture / index /\n  PEN_<n> / NONE uniformly.\n- object_animation: objectAnimTickDt — the driver''s accumulator\n  step is rate * +0xe0 * live-dtSec (DAT_0049b6f4), not a hardwired\n  1/30; objectAnimTick stays the locked-timing convention, twins\n  take the real frame dt.\n- freefall_runtime: kKurtHitFrames transcription fix — the latch\n  was 18 (the channel count); the record is 30 frames and the hit\n  site free-runs (+0x118=-1), so the latch is lround(acc)>=29, the\n  driver''s own frameCount-1 predicate. Digest-neutral (anim fields\n  are not hashed; verified).\n\nBridge (gdextension):\n- load_freefall(course, skill, seed) + get_mode; step_frame routes\n  mode 2 through the freefall core and runs the scene step with\n  the same dtSec; completion drives progressionFreefallHandoff\n  in-place — route 0 installs the traversal runtime and reuses the\n  shared presentTraversalLevel_ tail (factored out of load_level);\n  route 1 takes the frontend death route.\n- get_freefall_snapshot: phase/timeline/health/fade + the\n  FUN_004123f4 camera block (right=+X, down=-Y, boot zoom 2.4).\n- get_freefall_object_snapshots: the FUN_004109d8 active-list walk\n  — model tag, twin transform verbatim, driver-side anim fields,\n  chute attachment flag, geom_key.\n- get_freefall_object_geometry(slot, part): kind-2 meshes with\n  UVs + material grouping (part 1 = the +0x306 chute under the\n  object''s own basis.\n- get_freefall_material(name): palette-mapped ImageTexture,\n  palette-pen color, or the no-draw marker.\n- Traversal input/keyboard edge semantics shared via\n  buildRawInput_; traversal mode unchanged.\n\nGodot (main.tscn/main.gd):\n- FreefallRoot holds one node per presented pool slot; mesh\n  rebuilds gate on geom_key (anim churn), transforms applied\n  verbatim; chute attaches under the object basis; the FadeLayer/\n  FadeRect overlay presents the runtime fade (including the >1\n  flash); the camera takes the bridge transform + fov directly.\n- _process dispatches on bridge mode; the traversal tree hides\n  while mode 2 is live and restores after the handoff; the\n  FreefallRoot hides once mode leaves 2.\n- --freefall/--skill/--seed launcher args; the smoke runs\n  --smoke --freefall C --skill S --seed N.\n\nSmoke coverage (all 0 failures): course 0/2 hand off to mode 3;\ncourse 4 exercises the bones flyby and the health-gated death\nroute. Checks: Kurt model slot + animated-geometry churn,\nKURTANIM/KURT_HIT binding + sentinel rebind, orthonormal camera,\nCB3 texture + PEN fallback + unresolved-material paths, steering,\nfade, chute visibility, route consistency.\n\nCorrection folded in: the traversal smoke''s spawn-table check\nexpected K_IDLE — authored in 16B before the 16B.2 reroll port;\nthe seeded post-load roll lands the 95% branch so spawn posts\nK_STILL. Verified pre-existing at baseline (f52aa5f''s pytest was\n17+2 env-skips). The check now pins K_STILL.\n\nRegression: mdk_tests 5651/0, CTest 1/1, pytest 22/0 (canonical\nGodot binary), traversal LEVEL3-8 60f diag=0 with all six\ncanonical digests unchanged, freefall c0-c4 digests unchanged.\n\nDeferred seams (documented, not emulated): radar sprites (kind 1),\nBANG frame-block overlay (kind 3 — the variable-length frame\nencoding needs more RE), trails (kind 4), launch glows (kind 5),\nZOOM intro sprites, and all sounds. Explosion lifetime stays a\nbounded data seam.\n\nFREEFALL KURT GODOT PRESENTATION: CLOSED FOR BUILD_A\n\nGenerated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nEOF\n)","tree":{"sha":"1fcb39a1987b38c47f2f289d13627f0f125b3236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/git/trees/1fcb39a1987b38c47f2f289d13627f0f125b3236"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/git/commits/d0f9d8494aea1b765fd9dac27fcfa78f7375b82e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18028674?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kuh9325","id":18028674,"login":"kuh9325","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDI4Njc0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuh9325","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/commit/d0f9d8494aea1b765fd9dac27fcfa78f7375b82e","node_id":"C_kwDOUdj5udoAKGQwZjlkODQ5NGFlYTFiNzY1ZmQ5ZGFjMjdmY2ZhNzhmNzM3NWI4MmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/commit/8df701d324ef0bd367b7c5f6ce54b552f62c1c72","sha":"8df701d324ef0bd367b7c5f6ce54b552f62c1c72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kuh9325/MDK_Transplant/commits/8df701d324ef0bd367b7c5f6ce54b552f62c1c72"}],"sha":"d0f9d8494aea1b