riptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AVOAIML/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AVOAIML","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AVOAIML/delay-predictor/commits/7a3f609c89a0f04761be3ffaea101de8fbd6c80c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:48:28Z","email":"nimanthaavonet@gmail.com","name":"Nimantha Bandara"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:48:28Z","email":"nimanthaavonet@gmail.com","name":"Nimantha Bandara"},"message":"feat: ground Weight Agent LLM adjustment in recorded scoring history\n\nFeeds the cold-start weight-adjustment prompt a plain-text digest (fire\nrates, averages, judge-approval rate) built from recorded m3.snapshot.v1\nscoring runs, so the LLM reasons from this tenant''s actual observed\nsignals instead of the tenant description alone. Counts/averages only —\nno fitting, no coefficients; the LLM keeps full authority over the\nadjustment''s direction and magnitude.\n\nSnapshots are read through the existing medallion lake (LakeIO''s own\nfsspec-based LAKE_URI convention: MinIO locally, Azure Data Lake in the\ncloud), with a local-directory override for tests/demos. A storage or\nparse failure degrades to no digest, never a Weight Agent failure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"738512ac12b6ce148dc2b2f4e82fad1a29155438","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AVOAIML/delay-predictor/git/trees/738512ac12b6ce148dc2b2f4e82fad1a29155438"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AVOAIML/delay-predictor/git/commits/7a3f609c89a0f04761be3ffaea101de8fbd6c80c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/316418171?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AVOAIML/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AVOAIML/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AVOAIML